# Actual27 frozen-card → trained-deck diagnostic (not executed)

This stage uses the actual27 declarations and the inherited22-training/5-held
split. It does not replace them with synthetic bags. All1,432 copies/251 main
identities enter count-weighted, order-invariant aggregation, including unknown
card semantics. Leader/base, titles, source IDs and family IDs are provenance,
not feature inputs. Every near-clone/family remains in its inherited partition.

The old saved12 action-program bank covers zero actual main cards and is not
used as a whole-card bank. Runtime admission115IDs/635copies is a loader fact,
with game conformance unassessed. The proposed new whole-card bank covers only
eight actual IDs/65copies (4.539%): ASH_048, JTL_095, SEC_163, LOF_155, LOF_077,
JTL_078, JTL_158, JTL_217. LOF_155/JTL_217 are held from the new native card fit.
All remaining1,367 copies retain explicit unknown vectors. Eight decks have
zero bank-covered copies; retain and report them. Static whole-card serialization,
native-fixture evidence, learned-vector availability and trained-card status
are independent flags; none implies semantic validation or legal gameplay.

The whole-card stage reads complete pinned catalog rows, including intrinsic
keywords, printed stat modifiers and top-level attachment/executable fields.
Its finite fixture scope is disclosed by the card owner. Deck feature banks are
frozen snapshots of that stage's **final** correct-typed, untrained-typed and
ID-only16d vectors. No card weights are optimized here. Held-card native labels
never enter deck fit labels. No native intervention-profile objective is used.

The fourth arm uses each actual deck's already saved96d current-deck latent,
broadcast across its actual identity rows. No fresh baseline forward is needed.
The baseline had earlier composition training, and its historical objective and
compute are not matched. The new trainable readout graph and compute are matched.

Each identity row has130 inputs: semantic96 (zero-padded frozen16d or saved
baseline96); common32 printed fields; common bank-available and printed-known
flags. Printed32 is cost/power/hp÷10; unit/event/upgrade; ground/space; six aspects;
ten keywords; eight deterministic trait bins. Unsupported semantics use zero16.
Upgrade stat metadata uses explicit `upgradePower`/`upgradeHp` when present,
falling back to printed `power`/`hp` (including the real LOF_151+3/+2 case).
Unknown printed fields use zero32+known0. These flags never mean whole-card
semantic knowledge. Runtime/native/training masks are preserved in outputs and
reported as coverage, not fed as identity/partition proxies.

All four arms train the same6,829-parameter deck graph: φ130→32 GELU; copy-weighted
mean32 +sum32/60 +total/60 +distinct/60 +two copy-weighted coverage scalars;
ρ68→32 GELU; head32→13. Duplicate aliases merge first. Padding has copy weight0;
there is no live-card24-slot cap. Permuting rows or replacing duplicate rows by
their canonical summed count preserves the input bag; changing multiplicity
affects the sum/count features. The card bank itself is data, not Parameters.

Freeze seed17, one cloned initialization and one full22-row training batch in
every arm. AdamW(lr.003,betas.9/.999,eps1e-8,weight_decay0), exactly100 updates
per arm,400 total, no clipping/schedule/search/retry reset. Train shared MSE on
the training-only varying-target mask, which must be nonempty. All13 per-head
losses, constant flags, all13 MSE and varying-head macro are reported; regressions
and zero-covered-deck strata remain visible.

Targets are total/60, mean printed cost/10, low-cost≤2fraction, curve bins0…7/8+
fractions and unordered one-card unit probability. They are determined by shared
printed metadata/counts and **do not require card semantics**. Results test
composition/readout wiring and frozen-feature transfer only. Even a positive
result does not establish semantic deck quality, effect interactions, synergy,
action quality or game strength; these remain unsupported.

Initialization and fixed-final evaluation are one82-row batch each per arm,
eight batches total:27 original,27 reversed identity rows,27 duplicate-split
declarations merged back by canonical ID, and one source0 bag with one extra
copy of its lexically first main-card identity. The graph receives the same
canonical identity rows for duplicate splitting, preserving distinct-card count.
Actual predictions and32d latents must agree within1e-5 for permutations and
duplicate splitting; report the copy-perturbed output distance without forcing
it to be nonzero. Training excludes all metamorphic rows. Held metrics use only
the inherited five held original rows.
The cached current-deck96 vector stays fixed in these metamorphic rows; its
copy perturbation tests the new pooling/readout, without a fresh baseline
encoder call or a claim that cached deck96 updates when composition changes.
Final27×32ρ latents and predictions are saved from those same final calls, with no
extra export forward. A pure training22 target-mean constant baseline adds zero
NN/updates and reports all13/perhead/varying-macro held losses. Report family-first
held losses and the exact four held
families/five declarations, not27 independent validation examples. No checkpoint
or hyperparameter is selected from held metrics.

Execution requires root source/data/bank review and explicit GO. Deck allowance:
60 active wall seconds across every attempt,400 actual/reserved updates, eight
evaluation batches, oneCPU,1GiB sampled memory threshold, zero paid jobs/native
calls. Root serializes native90s/256calls, card60s/800updates/eight evaluations,
deck60s/400updates/eight evaluations and optional data-only30s,≤240 active seconds
in the shared `experiments/actual-corpus/campaign-ledger.jsonl`. Every completed
optimizer update is fsynced separately; failures retain time and reservation.

Source/data preparation imports no numerical framework. The frozen plan pins
coverage-v2, full catalog, inherited split, saved current96 export, card-bank
outputs and runner source. Exact source hashes are checked before/after the
worker. At this document's preparation stage native/model/deck work is pending;
no missing fixture or learned vector is upgraded to verified by this protocol.
